Rewritten: the provider profile itself (its default base of
https://api.groq.com/openai/v1, its GROQ_API_KEY variable, its fallback models
and its chat-completions wire) as a Nodecode catalog row and one request-body
hook; the per-model reasoning table, which sends each model only the
reasoning_effort values it was checked to accept and lowers a pick the model
does not take to the nearest weaker one (turning reasoning off sends `none'
where the model has it and its weakest level otherwise); and the filter that
keeps the models that cannot run a conversation out of the picker.

Added, because Nodecode's catalog is where a picker reads its list: the model
list is read from Groq's own /v1/models at start and hourly, since models.dev
publishes Groq under a package no Nodecode lane claims and names no address for
it -- without that row the provider could be neither chosen nor dialled.

Left out, and why: the Hermes private seams the original imported
(providers.base, ProviderProfile, register_provider) have no place here, so the
profile is a catalog row and its two methods (fetch_models,
build_api_kwargs_extras) are one /models read and one request-body hook. Hermes' 64K-token
context rule is not a Nodecode rule, so the filter keeps the original's own id
markers rather than a size ceiling, and a live model models.dev has not
published still lists (with Groq's rungs and no context or price) where Hermes
would have dropped it.
